{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:9e9bbf35ad61595b15a9e37566de2bc69d3e7afbb4fc20331ad37774c7646f0b","title":"Can a nonsingular Euclidean wormhole in a string background with a known CFT dual induce intrinsic randomness in couplings, even after the fundamental theory and vacuum are fixed? The proposed test requires localized wormhole ends that preserve the original boundary conditions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e2569cc0600f912a979c3c05ce2d9fcdac75cf5517c5f38898c2e36188a7b6d","title":"What soft supersymmetry-breaking parameters, weak-scale spectrum, electroweak breaking and gauge unification follow from the proposed fluxless G2 compactification framework?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9ed274efe4de46b0e3429e7ab2044f0386212a5acb47cfe61d28bb8a4d21e760","title":"Which dark-energy histories admit the positive-kinetic-energy scalar representation used by the excursion test? For positive scalar density, φ̇² = (1+w)ρφ requires w ≥ −1.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e323f468816f3aeb0eb0cdc7a0828e6bffaa1ed69be2389efbb91a36a9ec56e","title":"Can QED coupled to asymptotically safe Quantum Einstein Gravity possess an interacting continuum limit, avoid its Landau singularity, and predict the infrared electric charge rather than require it as an independent input?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e034da3ab98f163a1097b017c44c08a86ca85aa1efb90de3f2c7a3cba0f4943","title":"How can string theory provide symmetry protection, a trans-Planckian inflaton range and controlled moduli dynamics for large-field inflation, particularly axion monodromy, while connecting the construction to the scalar tilt n_s and tensor-to-scalar ratio r?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9edc38a925ca88966871d68630763c6b119e2204f652dc7fbc536f0232ec7308","title":"Can localized electric boundary forcing in four-dimensional asymptotically AdS Einstein–Maxwell theory drive smooth initial data toward arbitrarily large curvature visible to distant observers, providing a counterexample to the version of cosmic censorship considered here?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e4c982629edae1a599353e8a70daddfe81b1fed4aafd5629425ef4d1610119b","title":"Review how multiple inflaton fields generate cosmological perturbations, emphasizing field-space bases, gauge fixing, quadratic actions, power spectra, and nonlinear evolution.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e4ee80572d9dc345be728191bcd2673d2fc6e19d324d1293243493c10ce355b","title":"Under what spectrum and charge conditions does the exponentially suppressed one-loop cosmological constant of nonsupersymmetric Scherk–Schwarz heterotic models remain suppressed at two loops, and what might extend to higher orders?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e786dc287d555dea22e68bb4c6c2bf9480653907f335e58657e0e51dc92aab1","title":"Can LVS avoid the KKLT obstruction by allowing an effective superpotential parameter that need not be small, while retaining a light D7-position inflaton and a valid Kaluza–Klein cutoff?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e8132e79ed6ccf5a23f8ff3f6ef41ac328c67560b3370f8ba177b46124dbc12","title":"To what extent does the WGC constrain a low-energy EFT when its observers can create all subcutoff particles but may lack information about stable charged particles above its cutoff?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e2c601ae183a82279c890ca80372123d15173489d0df6dcae65cfa93d6c141b","title":"Determine whether early inflation, present dark energy and future expansion can obey simultaneous restrictions on scalar-field travel and positive-potential slope. The numerical strength of both restrictions remains an input rather than an established property of quantum gravity.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9eea79081da6b2b335c83a27e308ec06b1948c711f98859cea9c91f898d99f56","title":"Which observations could probe the light axions discussed here? The source highlights substructure, superradiance, and direct-detection experiments as prospective channels sensitive to axion mass and decay constant.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e46abd4882e7bf48a47df4758951dd560d509c2a6054ee9b6d4429ead7e2e56","title":"How do inflaton-dependent tower masses and thermal mass corrections enter dissipation and thermal corrections to an inflationary potential?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9ebc2cf7d7d878ac80b5084b5d5d450419cc253129cf1bc9dab73864be840032","title":"Can freeze-out during an early modulus-dominated era, followed by entropy dilution, reconcile photon-mediated millicharged DM with the fractional abundance needed in the paper's EDGES interpretation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e1a0cc363822941feab01110859b9fb83f0bcfe0196e148c166c303382fe51a","title":"How much expansion can occur before an initially Planck-scale wavelength reaches the Hubble radius? The TCC treats the avoidance of this crossing as a requirement on a cosmological EFT.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e1795051403851a0162b06690dd05ab823046570fa4563e51cea5e3f12b759c","title":"What additional group-theoretic structure distinguishes brane amplitudes of superconformal (2,2) theories from generic or massive (2,2) theories? The comparison fixes the topological pairing normalization and uses the superconformal R-charge grading.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e159759d6a0d6214e46d3c03d38df508e889f09dbfb114aa31d504a14ad835a","title":"Can random-matrix typicality explain the observed vacuum exclusions? The paper proposes a probabilistic origin for refined de Sitter and AdS scale restrictions within its selected flux model, motivated partly by earlier random-potential and entropic arguments.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0054"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e7a86a5dc1f81177274f4219e00d4fc9a0837f2bdd80922a6387b97cd9fedc8","title":"Can a unified treatment of classical type IIA flux potentials systematically classify extrema, their supersymmetry and perturbative stability, and the restrictions on de Sitter solutions and AdS scale separation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9ea27fea46a9e369480d460a1ae545038909a23309c8eece90d49fe36129a6b8","title":"How does an oscillating postinflationary equation of state affect a constant-mass spin-3/2 spectator? The scalar pressure repeatedly changes sign while its amplitude decays through cosmic expansion.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e374d14e3e7ee9789ef3ce441e4e02976faddcb7f4749cb83eaf26b5f3973c8","title":"Can microscopic vacua vary their cosmological constant independently of the gravitino mass, and would one or two towers govern those limits? The paper leaves this question open.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e478c759961427731f110d6cbcd91330fbc5bced3521eb1c6b3e99cb670f2ea","title":"How does the resonant Hamiltonian approximation organize long-time, small-amplitude bosonic dynamics in global AdS, including turbulent cascades, regular energy exchange, recurrences, and quantum diagnostics?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9ea8ce55135eeb6745c6e698c50b2cc94df463c116cd558a388639a3d63fabd3","title":"Are free BMN two-point functions with three string modes non-negative separately at every genus, as suggested by a proposed interpretation of normalized correlators as squared unitary transition amplitudes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9eab6d307f9733b0d42772f5172720319c2a08c89efd1123571c61c1b04c45c5","title":"Which parameter choices make toy no-scale supergravity de Sitter models compatible with the refined de Sitter conjecture (RdSC) and trans-Planckian censorship conjecture (TCC), and can added rolling fields stabilize the no-scale sector while retaining conjecture compatibility?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e787f67e8536ca580eba255b25a9a9d0d01e2f3bb478539a4f02f1c2cb20b74","title":"Would replacing all external 5-brane poles with 7-brane punctures exchange the roles of domain-wall expulsion and bubble nucleation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e8bb0e66181b98677f682bf2ca01ef96e4da29eac4847e337d00e46410d61e2","title":"Which localized codimension-one sources are compatible with string-inspired Einstein-dilaton vacua, and can their junction conditions, couplings and tensions admit a string interpretation when supersymmetry is absent?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0074"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9ecf978afe410630b76f16d17c2d4fb388ad37ecd29972125ad8cd82fdddde73","title":"Under what conditions can quantum fields and gravitational functional integrals accommodate spacetime topology changes and their associated singularities?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0078"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9ef0b089aa42978a8b81990cd7203752378adc6e688d4b949a9cc8f50686839d","title":"Can one explicitly enumerate all flux vacua at bounded flux number across the entire moduli space of a concrete type IIB orientifold, rather than sample fluxes or restrict to a boundary region?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9edbfbde8d941a491be7d1bccd19bbd11eb64b6442c5058b6394b2a6a5d8dd3b","title":"How do cross-couplings and repeated appearances of scalar fields in multiple exponential potential terms modify assisted power-law inflation, and under what conditions do the generalized potentials admit scaling solutions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0104"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:9e5952f58d1093b7e27464d4f68812d21a4f260a925be01f9666a58dfadb9e07","title":"Which dynamical supersymmetry-breaking scenarios can generate the weak/Planck hierarchy while satisfying particle phenomenology,